<section class="content-section product-detail-section content-section--tint"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading-page"><p class="section-kicker">BUYER'S GUIDE</p><h2>Field workforce software starts with the work pattern</h2><p>Field workforce software must match how your teams travel, visit sites and report activity. The right design depends on whether you need scheduled check-ins, visit records, attendance verification or location information—and how often that information is genuinely necessary.</p></div><div class="page-grid"><article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">01</span><h3>Define visibility requirements</h3><p>Specify what managers need to know, when records should be created and which events require a follow-up.</p></article>
<article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">02</span><h3>Set sensible location rules</h3><p>Confirm if location is captured only at defined actions or at other intervals. Explain tracking boundaries and access to staff.</p></article>
<article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">03</span><h3>Connect field activity to operations</h3><p>Map reporting needs, site records, employee identity, exceptions and any systems that must receive information.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="content-section product-faq-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading-page"><p class="section-kicker">PRODUCT QUESTIONS</p><h2>Questions to answer before choosing a solution</h2><p>Use these questions to check requirements and avoid assuming a feature, integration or operating model that has not been confirmed.</p></div><div class="faq-page-list"><details><summary>How is Timenox 360 different from Timenox?</summary><p>Timenox is positioned around attendance workflows, while Timenox 360 is intended for field-team and distributed operations use cases. Confirm the current feature set for each product before selection.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does the product track staff continuously?</summary><p>Do not assume continuous tracking. Confirm the exact location-capture behaviour, permitted times and device requirements for the intended deployment.</p></details>
<details><summary>What should field teams evaluate before rollout?</summary><p>Review phone compatibility, network conditions, location permissions, employee communications, site workflows and management reporting.</p></details>
